IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fhog-core`

-- First Home Owner Grant and Shared Equity Act 2000 (NSW) -- the first home owner grant, from the seat of the applicant.
--
-- SEAT: the applicant for the first home owner grant: a person buying or building a first home in New South Wales, with
-- or without one other person (a spouse or de facto partner, or a co-applicant). "Am I eligible? Is this home an eligible
-- transaction under the cap? How much is the grant? By when must I apply? What must I do, and by when, if a condition
-- fails, and what can be recovered?" Every question is phrased as that person asks it, on facts that person could state.
-- The rules are in fhog-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- The questions take their inputs in one order: the transaction, then you, then the other person, then the other owners.
-- A question that involves other people answers `not covered` if there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de
-- facto partner of either of you: the core takes any number, but these questions ask about two people.
--
-- Edition: act-2000-021 (corpus version 2023-09-04), from the Open Australian Legal Corpus as at 10 March 2025. NOT THE
-- CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT AND MAY BE OUT OF DATE. The eligibility caps are the s 13A(2) figures unless you say a regulation
-- under s 13A(4) sets another (none is deposited); a regulation would change the answers.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The first home owner grant -- the applicant's questions`

§§ `Plain answers, and the records built from them`

-- One question about the past, asked of you or of the other person. Pick New South Wales if it happened there and also
-- elsewhere.
DECLARE `What happened` IS ONE OF
    `no`
    `yes, in New South Wales`
    `yes, in another State or a Territory, and it counts under that place's law`
    `yes, in another State or a Territory, and I am not sure whether it counts under that place's law`

GIVEN `w` IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it happened in New South Wales` IF
    CONSIDER `w`
    WHEN `yes, in New South Wales` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `w` IS A `What happened`
GIVETH AN `Interstate fact`
`the interstate part of` `w` MEANS
    CONSIDER `w`
    WHEN `yes, in another State or a Territory, and it counts under that place's law` THEN `applies under the corresponding law`
    WHEN `yes, in another State or a Territory, and I am not sure whether it counts under that place's law` THEN `depends on the corresponding law`
    OTHERWISE `does not apply`

GIVEN `earlier grant` IS A `What happened`
      `paid back` IS A BOOLEAN
      `interest before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened`
      `interest and 6 months' residence` IS A `What happened`
GIVETH AN `Earlier history`
`a history from` `earlier grant` `paid back` `interest before 1 July 2000` `interest and 6 months' residence` MEANS
    `Earlier history` WITH
        `a party to an earlier application under this Act on which a grant was paid`            IS `it happened in New South Wales` `earlier grant`
        `a party to an earlier application under a corresponding law on which a grant was paid` IS `the interstate part of` `earlier grant`
        `every such grant was paid back with any penalty payable under s 45`                    IS `paid back`
        `held a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales before 1 July 2000` IS `it happened in New South Wales` `interest before 1 July 2000`
        `held a relevant interest in residential property elsewhere in Australia before 1 July 2000` IS `the interstate part of` `interest before 1 July 2000`
        `held a relevant interest in residential property in New South Wales and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS `it happened in New South Wales` `interest and 6 months' residence`
        `held a relevant interest in residential property elsewhere in Australia and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS `the interstate part of` `interest and 6 months' residence`

GIVEN `lives there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `began on` IS A DATE
      `months` IS A NUMBER
      `later start approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `shorter stay approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Residence`
`a residence from` `lives there` `began on` `months` `later start approved` `shorter stay approved` `exempted` MEANS
    `Residence` WITH
        `occupies the home as principal place of residence`                            IS `lives there`
        `the date occupation began`                                                    IS `began on`
        `continuous months of occupation`                                              IS `months`
        `the Chief Commissioner approved the later start`                              IS `later start approved`
        `the Chief Commissioner approved the shorter period`                           IS `shorter stay approved`
        `the Chief Commissioner exempted the applicant from the residence requirement` IS `exempted`

-- The relationship between you and the other person, as s 6 asks it. Listed as a partner only if married or de facto;
-- the core decides whether that makes a spouse (s 6(2)).
GIVEN `married` IS A BOOLEAN, `de facto` IS A BOOLEAN, `apart` IS A BOOLEAN, `their history` IS AN `Earlier history`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Partner`
`the partners from` `married` `de facto` `apart` `their history` MEANS
    IF `married` OR `de facto`
    THEN LIST (`Partner` WITH
                  `is legally married to the applicant on the commencement date`          IS `married`
                  `is the applicant's de facto partner on the commencement date`          IS `de facto`
                  `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that they were not cohabiting and will not resume` IS `apart`
                  `the partner's history`                                                 IS `their history`)
    ELSE EMPTY

-- `is a natural person` is TRUE: the seat is an individual (s 8 is tested in the core cases).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `age exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `status` IS A `Status on the commencement date`
      `history` IS AN `Earlier history`
      `partners` IS A LIST OF `Partner`
      `residence` IS A `Residence`
GIVETH AN `Applicant`
`an applicant from` `age` `age exemption` `status` `history` `partners` `residence` MEANS
    `Applicant` WITH
        `is a natural person`               IS TRUE
        `age when applying`                 IS `age`
        `exempted from the age requirement` IS `age exemption`
        `status`                            IS `status`
        `the applicant's history`           IS `history`
        `the applicant's partners`          IS `partners`
        `the applicant's residence`         IS `residence`

-- The transaction, from the answers about it.
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `in NSW` IS A BOOLEAN
      `commencement` IS A DATE
      `completion` IS A DATE
      `completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `origin` IS AN `Origin of the home`
      `occupied or sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `demolished premises occupied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `old option` IS A BOOLEAN
      `replaces` IS A `Replaced contract`
      `transitional option` IS A BOOLEAN
      `consideration` IS A NUMBER
      `unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
      `land consideration` IS A NUMBER
      `land unencumbered value` IS A NUMBER
      `regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulation cap` IS A NUMBER
      `already paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transaction`
`a transaction from` `kind` `in NSW` `commencement` `completion` `completed` `origin` `occupied or sold` `demolished premises occupied` `owner of the land` `old option` `replaces` `transitional option` `consideration` `unencumbered value` `land consideration` `land unencumbered value` `regulation` `regulation cap` `already paid` MEANS
    `Transaction` WITH
        `kind`                                                           IS `kind`
        `the home is in New South Wales`                                 IS `in NSW`
        `the commencement date`                                          IS `commencement`
        `the completion date`                                            IS `completion`
        `has been completed`                                             IS `completed`
        `origin of the home`                                             IS `origin`
        `the home has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS `occupied or sold`
        `the owner occupied the demolished premises`                     IS `demolished premises occupied`
        `the person building is or will on completion be the owner of the land` IS `owner of the land`
        `an option or right granted before 1 July 2000 applies`          IS `old option`
        `replaced contract`                                              IS `replaces`
        `made pursuant to an option granted in the transitional period`  IS `transitional option`
        `the consideration`                                              IS `consideration`
        `the unencumbered value of the property or home`                 IS `unencumbered value`
        `the consideration for the land`                                 IS `land consideration`
        `the unencumbered value of the land`                             IS `land unencumbered value`
        `cap regulation`                                                 IS `the cap regulation from` `regulation` `regulation cap`
        `a grant has already been paid for this transaction`             IS `already paid`

-- s 13A(4): a regulation's cap, if you know it; 0 if you know there is one but not its amount.
GIVEN `regulation` IS A BOOLEAN, `regulation cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Cap regulation`
`the cap regulation from` `regulation` `regulation cap` MEANS
    IF `regulation`
    THEN IF `regulation cap` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `a regulation under s 13A(4) prescribes` `regulation cap`
         ELSE `a regulation under s 13A(4) applies but its amount is not known`
    ELSE `no regulation under s 13A(4) applies`

-- The two people: you, and (if there is one) the other person. Each is the other's partner when married or de facto.
GIVEN `me` IS AN `Applicant`, `the other person` IS AN `Applicant`, `the other person applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Applicant`
`the applicants from` `me` `the other person` `the other person applies` MEANS
    IF `the other person applies`
    THEN LIST `me`, `the other person`
    ELSE LIST `me`

-- A question about two people answers `not covered` if there is someone further.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE, `someone else` IS A BOOLEAN, `the answer` IS AN `Answer` a
GIVETH AN `Answer` a
`unless there is someone else` `someone else` `the answer` MEANS
    IF `someone else`
    THEN `not covered` `the application has more applicants, spouses or de facto partners than this question asks about`
    ELSE `the answer`

§§ `s 6, s 4A, s 5, s 15 -- who and what counts`

@export Is this person my spouse for the first home owner grant (s 6)?
GIVEN `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other person are legally married on the commencement date (the day the contract is made, or the day the foundations are begun for an owner build)
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your de facto partner on the commencement date (as defined in s 21C of the Interpretation Act 1987)
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are legally married: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that you were not living together on the commencement date, are not now, and do not intend to resume (s 6(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my spouse for the grant` IF
    `they are spouses` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume`

@export Is the home a new home for the first home owner grant (s 4A)?
GIVEN `how the home came to be` IS AN `Origin of the home` @desc Whether the home is an ordinary home, a substantially renovated home (all or substantially all of a building removed or replaced), or a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land
      `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as it now stands (as renovated, or as rebuilt), has ever been lived in or sold as a place of residence
      `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a home built to replace demolished premises: whether the owner lived in the old home as a place of residence before it was demolished
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home a new home` IF
    `it is a new home` `how the home came to be` `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises`

@export Is my interest in the land a relevant interest, so that I am an owner of the home (s 5)?
GIVEN `my interest in the land` IS A `Kind of interest in land` @desc What you hold or will hold in the land: usually an estate in fee simple (freehold, including a strata lot); choose an option that needs the Chief Commissioner only if the Chief Commissioner has approved, is satisfied, or is of that opinion
      `I will have a right to immediate occupation within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or will have within 12 months (or a longer time the Chief Commissioner allows), a right to move in straight away
      `I hold it on trust for someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the interest subject to a trust (as a trustee)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my interest a relevant interest` IF
    `it is a relevant interest` `my interest in the land` `I will have a right to immediate occupation within 12 months` `I hold it on trust for someone else`

@export Can my application go ahead without the owners who are not applying (s 15)?
GIVEN `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest ownership share, in per cent, of any person who will own part of the home but is not applying (0 if every owner applies); leave out the NSW Land and Housing Corporation and an approved shared equity partner
      `the total share of all owners with 5% or less` IS A NUMBER @desc The total ownership share, in per cent, of every owner (applying or not) whose own share is 5% or less
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my application go ahead without the other owners` IF
    `every owner who is not applying is excluded from being an interested person` `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` `the total share of all owners with 5% or less`

§§ `ss 13, 13AA, 13A, 13B -- my transaction`

@export Is my purchase, building contract or owner build an eligible transaction (s 13)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract (including off the plan), having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is in New South Wales
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `how the home came to be` IS AN `Origin of the home` @desc Whether the home is an ordinary home, a substantially renovated home, or a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land
      `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as it now stands, has ever been lived in or sold as a place of residence
      `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a home built to replace demolished premises: whether the owner lived in the old home before it was demolished
      `I am or will be the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a building contract or an owner build: whether you own the land, or will own it when the contract is completed
      `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract was made under an option, or a right to require it, granted before 1 July 2000
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract` @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier one for the same home (or a substantially similar home), and when that earlier contract was made
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` IS
    `is an eligible transaction` (`a transaction from` `what I am doing` `the home is in New South Wales` `the commencement date` `the commencement date` FALSE `how the home came to be` `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` `I am or will be the owner of the land` `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE)
    -- The completion date, completion, transitional option, values, regulation and earlier grant are not read by s 13:
    -- fixed placeholders.

@export Which first home owner grant is available for my transaction: the builder's grant or the purchaser's grant (s 13AA)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract, having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
GIVETH A `Type of grant`
DECIDE `Which grant is available for my transaction` IS
    `the type of grant available for` (`a transaction from` `what I am doing` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) FALSE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE)
    -- Only the kind is read by s 13AA: the rest are fixed placeholders.

@export What is the eligibility cap for my transaction (s 13A)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract, having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract` @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier one for the same home (or a substantially similar home), and when that earlier contract was made
      `a regulation sets a different cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap for your transaction (if unsure, answer no: the Act's figures are then used)
      `the cap that regulation sets` IS A NUMBER @desc The cap that regulation sets, in dollars (0 if you do not know it)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` IS
    `the eligibility cap for` (`a transaction from` `what I am doing` TRUE `the commencement date` `the commencement date` FALSE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 `a regulation sets a different cap` `the cap that regulation sets` FALSE)
    -- Only the kind, commencement date, replacement and regulation are read by s 13A: the rest are fixed placeholders.

@export What is the total value of my transaction, the figure tested against the cap (s 13B)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract, having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc The price under the contract; for a building contract the total price of the building work; for an owner build your actual costs, leaving out any allowance for your own labour (dollars)
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc For a purchase, the full value of the property on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, the full value of the home when it is ready to live in; ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement to lower the value (dollars; 0 for a building contract)
      `what I paid or must pay for the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract or an owner build, what you paid or must pay for the land (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `the unencumbered value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract, the land's full value on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, on the day the home is ready to live in (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the total value of my transaction` IS
    `the total value of` (`a transaction from` `what I am doing` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) FALSE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE `the consideration` `the unencumbered value of the home` `what I paid or must pay for the land` `the unencumbered value of the land` FALSE 0 FALSE)
    -- Only the kind and the values are read by s 13B: the rest are fixed placeholders.

@export Is the total value of my transaction within the eligibility cap (ss 7(1)(c), 13A, 13B)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract, having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract` @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier one for the same home (or a substantially similar home), and when that earlier contract was made
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc The price under the contract; for a building contract the total price of the building work; for an owner build your actual costs, leaving out any allowance for your own labour (dollars)
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc For a purchase, the full value of the property on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, the full value of the home when it is ready to live in (dollars; 0 for a building contract)
      `what I paid or must pay for the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract or an owner build, what you paid or must pay for the land (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `the unencumbered value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract, the land's full value on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, on the day the home is ready to live in (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `a regulation sets a different cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap for your transaction (if unsure, answer no)
      `the cap that regulation sets` IS A NUMBER @desc The cap that regulation sets, in dollars (0 if you do not know it)
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my transaction within the cap` IS
    `the total value is within the eligibility cap for` (`a transaction from` `what I am doing` TRUE `the commencement date` `the commencement date` FALSE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` FALSE `the consideration` `the unencumbered value of the home` `what I paid or must pay for the land` `the unencumbered value of the land` `a regulation sets a different cap` `the cap that regulation sets` FALSE)
    -- The other facts are not read by s 13A or s 13B: fixed placeholders.

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 -- am I eligible`

@export Am I old enough for the first home owner grant (s 8A)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when you apply
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted you from having to be 18 (s 8A(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough` IF
    `criterion 1A is met by` (`an applicant from` `my age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` `none of these` (`a history from` `no` FALSE `no` `no`) EMPTY (`a residence from` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    -- Only the age and exemption are read by s 8A: the rest are fixed placeholders.

@export Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion (s 9)?
GIVEN `my status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc Whether, on the commencement date, you were an Australian citizen, held a permanent visa, or were a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person is applying for the grant with you
      `the other person's status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc If so, the other person's status on the commencement date
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else`
        (`known` (`criterion 2 is met by` `me` `among` (`the applicants from` `me` `the other person` `the other person is applying with me`)))
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `my status on the commencement date` `a clean history` EMPTY `no residence`
        `the other person` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `the other person's status on the commencement date` `a clean history` EMPTY `no residence`
        `a clean history` MEANS `a history from` `no` FALSE `no` `no`
        `no residence` MEANS `a residence from` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE
        -- Only the statuses are read by s 9: age, history and residence are fixed placeholders.

@export Am I free of the bar on a second grant -- has no earlier grant been paid to me or my spouse and not paid back (s 10)?
GIVEN `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application you were a party to, under this Act (New South Wales) or another State's or Territory's first home owner grant law
      `I paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant was later paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other person are legally married on the commencement date
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your de facto partner on the commencement date
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are legally married: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied of the s 6(2) separation
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc The same question about the other person
      `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant to the other person was paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I free of the second grant bar` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else` (`criterion 3 is met by` `me`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `an Australian citizen` (`a history from` `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` `I paid that grant back with any penalty` `no` `no`) (`the partners from` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` (`a history from` `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` `no` `no`)) `no residence`
        `no residence` MEANS `a residence from` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE
        -- s 10 reads only the earlier grants and who is a spouse: the rest are fixed placeholders.

@export Have neither I nor my spouse held a home that counts against a first home owner (s 11)?
GIVEN `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether you ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest (such as freehold) in land with a home on it, anywhere in Australia, whether or not you lived there
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, you held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row (ignore any delay in moving in because it was leased)
      `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other person are legally married on the commencement date
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your de facto partner on the commencement date
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are legally married: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied of the s 6(2) separation
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc The same question about the other person
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc The same question about the other person
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I never held a home that counts` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else` (`criterion 4 is met by` `me`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `an Australian citizen` (`a history from` `no` FALSE `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months`) (`the partners from` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` (`a history from` `no` FALSE `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months`)) `no residence`
        `no residence` MEANS `a residence from` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2017) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE
        -- s 11 reads only the earlier interests and who is a spouse: the rest are fixed placeholders.

@export Do I meet the residence requirement -- moving in within 12 months of completion and living there 12 months in a row (s 12)?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction is (or is expected to be) completed: for a purchase, when you are entitled to possession and your title is registered; for building, when the home is ready to live in
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as your main home
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day you began, or will begin, living in the home as your main home
      `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row you have lived, or will live, in the home as your main home
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your moving in more than 12 months after completion (s 12(3)(a))
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your living there for less than 12 months (s 12(3)(b))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted you from the residence requirement (s 12(4))
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person is applying for the grant with you
      `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the other person has moved in, or will move in, as their main home
      `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day the other person began, or will begin, living in the home
      `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row the other person has lived, or will live, there
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the residence requirement` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else`
        (`known` (`criterion 5 is met by` `me` `among` (`the applicants from` `me` `the other person` `the other person is applying with me`) `completing on` `the completion date`))
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `an Australian citizen` `a clean history` EMPTY (`a residence from` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement`)
        `the other person` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `an Australian citizen` `a clean history` EMPTY (`a residence from` `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement`)
        `a clean history` MEANS `a history from` `no` FALSE `no` `no`
        -- s 12 reads only the residence facts: age, status and history are fixed placeholders.

§§ `ss 7 and 18 -- is the grant payable, and how much`

-- The whole application from the plain answers: the transaction, you, the other person, the other owners.
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `the home is in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE
      `the completion date` IS A DATE
      `the transaction has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the home came to be` IS AN `Origin of the home`
      `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am or will be the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract`
      `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER
      `what I paid or must pay for the land` IS A NUMBER
      `the unencumbered value of the land` IS A NUMBER
      `a regulation sets a different cap` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cap that regulation sets` IS A NUMBER
      `a grant has already been paid for this transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date`
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` IS A `What happened`
      `I paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened`
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened`
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE
      `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person's status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date`
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` IS A `What happened`
      `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened`
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened`
      `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE
      `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` IS A NUMBER
      `the total share of all owners with 5% or less` IS A NUMBER
      `the Chief Commissioner authorised payment before completion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application`
`the application from my answers` MEANS
    `Application` WITH
        `the applicants`                                                  IS `the applicants from` `me` `the other person` `the other person is applying with me`
        `the transaction`                                                 IS `the transaction`
        `the largest ownership share of an owner who is not applying`     IS `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying`
        `the total ownership share of all small interest holders`         IS `the total share of all owners with 5% or less`
        `the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment before completion` IS `the Chief Commissioner authorised payment before completion`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `a transaction from` `what I am doing` `the home is in New South Wales` `the commencement date` `the completion date` `the transaction has been completed` `how the home came to be` `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` `I am or will be the owner of the land` `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` `the consideration` `the unencumbered value of the home` `what I paid or must pay for the land` `the unencumbered value of the land` `a regulation sets a different cap` `the cap that regulation sets` `a grant has already been paid for this transaction`
        `my history` MEANS `a history from` `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` `I paid that grant back with any penalty` `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months`
        `the other person's history` MEANS `a history from` `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months`
