        `the other person` MEANS `an applicant from` `the other person's age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` `the other person's status on the commencement date` `the other person's history` (`the partners from` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` `my history`) (`a residence from` `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement`)

§§ `ss 7, 8 to 12 and 18 -- am I eligible, is the grant payable, and how much`

-- Every criterion in Part 2 Division 2, for you (s 7(1)(a), (2)). It reads the people and the completion date.
@export Am I eligible for the first home owner grant -- do I meet every eligibility criterion (ss 8 to 12)?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction is (or is expected to be) completed: for a purchase, when you are entitled to possession and your title is registered; for building, when the home is ready to live in
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when you apply
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted you from having to be 18 (s 8A(2))
      `my status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc Whether, on the commencement date, you were an Australian citizen, held a permanent visa, or were a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application you were a party to, under this Act (New South Wales) or another State's or Territory's first home owner grant law
      `I paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant was later paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether you ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest (such as freehold) in land with a home on it, whether or not you lived there
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, you held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row (ignore any delay in moving in because it was leased)
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as your main home
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day you began, or will begin, living in the home as your main home
      `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row you have lived, or will live, in the home as your main home
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your moving in more than 12 months after completion (s 12(3)(a))
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your living there for less than 12 months (s 12(3)(b))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted you from the residence requirement (s 12(4))
      `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other person (if there is one) are legally married on the commencement date
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your de facto partner on the commencement date (as defined in s 21C of the Interpretation Act 1987)
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are legally married: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that you were not living together on the commencement date, are not now, and do not intend to resume (s 6(2))
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is applying for the grant with you
      `the other person's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other person's age in years when applying
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted the other person from having to be 18
      `the other person's status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc The other person's citizenship or visa status on the commencement date
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application the other person was a party to, in New South Wales or elsewhere
      `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant to the other person was paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether the other person ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest in land with a home on it
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, the other person held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row
      `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person has moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as their main home
      `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day the other person began, or will begin, living in the home
      `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row the other person has lived, or will live, there
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's moving in more than 12 months after completion
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's living there for less than 12 months
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person (these questions then answer not covered)
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else` (`the eligibility criteria are met by` `me` `on` `the application`)
    WHERE
        `the application` MEANS `the application from my answers` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `the completion date` `the completion date` TRUE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE `my age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` `my status on the commencement date` `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` `I paid that grant back with any penalty` `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` `the other person is applying with me` `the other person's age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` `the other person's status on the commencement date` `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` 0 0 FALSE
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from` `my age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` `my status on the commencement date` (`a history from` `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` `I paid that grant back with any penalty` `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months`) (`the partners from` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` (`a history from` `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months`)) (`a residence from` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement`)
        -- Only the people and the completion date are read by ss 8 to 12: the other facts are fixed placeholders.

@export Is the first home owner grant payable on my application (s 7)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract (including off the plan), having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is in New South Wales
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction is (or is expected to be) completed: for a purchase, when you are entitled to possession and your title is registered; for building, when the home is ready to live in
      `the transaction has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that day has come and the transaction is completed
      `how the home came to be` IS AN `Origin of the home` @desc Whether the home is an ordinary home, a substantially renovated home (all or substantially all of a building removed or replaced), or a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land
      `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as it now stands (as renovated, or as rebuilt), has ever been lived in or sold as a place of residence
      `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a home built to replace demolished premises: whether the owner lived in the old home as a place of residence before it was demolished
      `I am or will be the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a building contract or an owner build: whether you own the land, or will own it when the contract is completed
      `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract was made under an option, or a right to require it, granted before 1 July 2000
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract` @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier one for the same home (or a substantially similar home), and when that earlier contract was made
      `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a purchase or building contract was made under an option or right granted in the 2012 transitional period (from the day the 2012 Budget Measures Bill was introduced to 30 September 2012)
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc The price under the contract; for a building contract the total price of the building work; for an owner build your actual costs, leaving out any allowance for your own labour (dollars)
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc For a purchase, the full value of the property on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, the full value of the home when it is ready to live in; ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement to lower the value (dollars; 0 for a building contract)
      `what I paid or must pay for the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract or an owner build, what you paid or must pay for the land (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `the unencumbered value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract, the land's full value on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, on the day the home is ready to live in (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `a regulation sets a different cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap for your transaction (if unsure, answer no: the Act's figures are then used)
      `the cap that regulation sets` IS A NUMBER @desc The cap that regulation sets, in dollars (0 if you do not know it)
      `a grant has already been paid for this transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has already been paid for this same purchase or building (only one grant is payable for a transaction)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when you apply
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted you from having to be 18 (s 8A(2))
      `my status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc Whether, on the commencement date, you were an Australian citizen, held a permanent visa, or were a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application you were a party to, under this Act (New South Wales) or another State's or Territory's first home owner grant law
      `I paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant was later paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether you ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest (such as freehold) in land with a home on it, whether or not you lived there
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, you held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row (ignore any delay in moving in because it was leased)
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as your main home
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day you began, or will begin, living in the home as your main home
      `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row you have lived, or will live, in the home as your main home
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your moving in more than 12 months after completion (s 12(3)(a))
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your living there for less than 12 months (s 12(3)(b))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted you from the residence requirement (s 12(4))
      `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other person (if there is one) are legally married on the commencement date
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your de facto partner on the commencement date (as defined in s 21C of the Interpretation Act 1987)
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are legally married: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that you were not living together on the commencement date, are not now, and do not intend to resume (s 6(2))
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is applying for the grant with you
      `the other person's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other person's age in years when applying
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted the other person from having to be 18
      `the other person's status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc The other person's citizenship or visa status on the commencement date
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application the other person was a party to, in New South Wales or elsewhere
      `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant to the other person was paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether the other person ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest in land with a home on it
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, the other person held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row
      `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person has moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as their main home
      `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day the other person began, or will begin, living in the home
      `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row the other person has lived, or will live, there
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's moving in more than 12 months after completion
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's living there for less than 12 months
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person (these questions then answer not covered)
      `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest ownership share, in per cent, of any person who will own part of the home but is not applying (0 if every owner applies); leave out the NSW Land and Housing Corporation and an approved shared equity partner
      `the total share of all owners with 5% or less` IS A NUMBER @desc The total ownership share, in per cent, of every owner (applying or not) whose own share is 5% or less
      `the Chief Commissioner authorised payment before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment of the grant before completion (s 20(1)(a))
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the grant payable on my application` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else` (`the grant is payable on` (`the application from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in New South Wales` `the commencement date` `the completion date` `the transaction has been completed` `how the home came to be` `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` `I am or will be the owner of the land` `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` `the consideration` `the unencumbered value of the home` `what I paid or must pay for the land` `the unencumbered value of the land` `a regulation sets a different cap` `the cap that regulation sets` `a grant has already been paid for this transaction` `my age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` `my status on the commencement date` `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` `I paid that grant back with any penalty` `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` `the other person is applying with me` `the other person's age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` `the other person's status on the commencement date` `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` `the total share of all owners with 5% or less` `the Chief Commissioner authorised payment before completion`))

@export How much first home owner grant will be paid on my application (ss 7 and 18)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract (including off the plan), having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is in New South Wales
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction is (or is expected to be) completed: for a purchase, when you are entitled to possession and your title is registered; for building, when the home is ready to live in
      `the transaction has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that day has come and the transaction is completed
      `how the home came to be` IS AN `Origin of the home` @desc Whether the home is an ordinary home, a substantially renovated home (all or substantially all of a building removed or replaced), or a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land
      `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as it now stands (as renovated, or as rebuilt), has ever been lived in or sold as a place of residence
      `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a home built to replace demolished premises: whether the owner lived in the old home as a place of residence before it was demolished
      `I am or will be the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a building contract or an owner build: whether you own the land, or will own it when the contract is completed
      `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract was made under an option, or a right to require it, granted before 1 July 2000
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract` @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier one for the same home (or a substantially similar home), and when that earlier contract was made
      `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a purchase or building contract was made under an option or right granted in the 2012 transitional period (from the day the 2012 Budget Measures Bill was introduced to 30 September 2012)
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc The price under the contract; for a building contract the total price of the building work; for an owner build your actual costs, leaving out any allowance for your own labour (dollars)
      `the unencumbered value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc For a purchase, the full value of the property on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, the full value of the home when it is ready to live in; ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement to lower the value (dollars; 0 for a building contract)
      `what I paid or must pay for the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract or an owner build, what you paid or must pay for the land (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `the unencumbered value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc For a building contract, the land's full value on the day the contract was made; for an owner build, on the day the home is ready to live in (dollars; 0 for a purchase)
      `a regulation sets a different cap` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap for your transaction (if unsure, answer no: the Act's figures are then used)
      `the cap that regulation sets` IS A NUMBER @desc The cap that regulation sets, in dollars (0 if you do not know it)
      `a grant has already been paid for this transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has already been paid for this same purchase or building (only one grant is payable for a transaction)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years when you apply
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted you from having to be 18 (s 8A(2))
      `my status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc Whether, on the commencement date, you were an Australian citizen, held a permanent visa, or were a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application you were a party to, under this Act (New South Wales) or another State's or Territory's first home owner grant law
      `I paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant was later paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether you ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest (such as freehold) in land with a home on it, whether or not you lived there
      `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, you held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row (ignore any delay in moving in because it was leased)
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as your main home
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day you began, or will begin, living in the home as your main home
      `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row you have lived, or will live, in the home as your main home
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your moving in more than 12 months after completion (s 12(3)(a))
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your living there for less than 12 months (s 12(3)(b))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted you from the residence requirement (s 12(4))
      `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other person (if there is one) are legally married on the commencement date
      `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is your de facto partner on the commencement date (as defined in s 21C of the Interpretation Act 1987)
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are legally married: whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied that you were not living together on the commencement date, are not now, and do not intend to resume (s 6(2))
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is applying for the grant with you
      `the other person's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other person's age in years when applying
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has exempted the other person from having to be 18
      `the other person's status on the commencement date` IS A `Status on the commencement date` @desc The other person's citizenship or visa status on the commencement date
      `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether a first home owner grant was ever paid on an earlier application the other person was a party to, in New South Wales or elsewhere
      `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every such grant to the other person was paid back, with any penalty under s 45
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether the other person ever held, before 1 July 2000, a relevant interest in land with a home on it
      `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` IS A `What happened` @desc Whether, before the commencement date, the other person held a relevant interest in land with a home on it and lived there for at least 6 months in a row
      `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person has moved in, or will move in, to live in the home as their main home
      `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day the other person began, or will begin, living in the home
      `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row the other person has lived, or will live, there
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's moving in more than 12 months after completion
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's living there for less than 12 months
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a further applicant, or another spouse or de facto partner of you or the other person (these questions then answer not covered)
      `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` IS A NUMBER @desc The largest ownership share, in per cent, of any person who will own part of the home but is not applying (0 if every owner applies); leave out the NSW Land and Housing Corporation and an approved shared equity partner
      `the total share of all owners with 5% or less` IS A NUMBER @desc The total ownership share, in per cent, of every owner (applying or not) whose own share is 5% or less
      `the Chief Commissioner authorised payment before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment of the grant before completion (s 20(1)(a))
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `How much grant will be paid on my application` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else` (`the grant payable on` (`the application from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in New South Wales` `the commencement date` `the completion date` `the transaction has been completed` `how the home came to be` `the home has been occupied or sold as a place of residence` `an owner of the home lived in the demolished premises` `I am or will be the owner of the land` `an option granted before 1 July 2000 applies` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` `the consideration` `the unencumbered value of the home` `what I paid or must pay for the land` `the unencumbered value of the land` `a regulation sets a different cap` `the cap that regulation sets` `a grant has already been paid for this transaction` `my age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the age requirement` `my status on the commencement date` `an earlier grant was paid on an application I was party to` `I paid that grant back with any penalty` `I held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `I held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` `the other person is legally married to me on the commencement date` `the other person is my de facto partner on the commencement date` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied we were not living together and will not resume` `the other person is applying with me` `the other person's age` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the age requirement` `the other person's status on the commencement date` `an earlier grant was paid on an application the other person was party to` `the other person paid that grant back with any penalty` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` `the other person held a relevant interest in residential property and lived in it for 6 continuous months` `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` `the largest share held by an owner who is not applying` `the total share of all owners with 5% or less` `the Chief Commissioner authorised payment before completion`))

@export How much is the first home owner grant for my transaction, if it is payable (s 18)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc Whether you are buying a home under a contract (including off the plan), having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building it yourself as an owner builder
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` IS A `Replaced contract` @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier one for the same home (or a substantially similar home), and when that earlier contract was made
      `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a purchase or building contract was made under an option or right granted in the 2012 transitional period (from the day the 2012 Budget Measures Bill was introduced to 30 September 2012)
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc The price under the contract; for a building contract the total price of the building work; for an owner build your actual costs, leaving out any allowance for your own labour (dollars)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the grant for my transaction` IS
    `the amount of the grant for` (`a transaction from` `what I am doing` TRUE `the commencement date` `the commencement date` TRUE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied it replaces an earlier contract` `it was made under an option granted in the transitional period` `the consideration` 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE)
    -- Only the kind, commencement date, replacement, transitional option and consideration are read by s 18: the
    -- other facts are fixed placeholders.

§§ `s 14(5), (6) -- when I may apply`

@export By when must I apply for the first home owner grant (s 14(5))?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction is (or is expected to be) completed: for a purchase, when you are entitled to possession and your title is registered; for building, when the home is ready to live in
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply` IS
    `the application period ends on` (`a transaction from` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `the completion date` `the completion date` TRUE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE)
    -- Only the completion date is read by s 14(5)(b): the other facts are fixed placeholders.

@export Is my application for the first home owner grant made in time (s 14(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction is (or is expected to be) completed
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) the application
      `the Chief Commissioner allows my application outside the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has used the s 14(6) discretion to allow your application before or after the application period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application in time` IF
    `the application may be made on` `the day I apply` `for` (`a transaction from` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `the commencement date` `the completion date` TRUE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE) `if allowed` `the Chief Commissioner allows my application outside the period`
    -- Only the two dates are read by s 14(5): the other facts are fixed placeholders.

§§ `ss 20 and 21 -- if I was paid early and a condition fails`

-- These questions arise only if the grant was paid to you in advance: before completion (s 20(2)), in anticipation of the
-- eligibility cap (s 20(2A)), or before you had met the residence requirement (s 20(3)). The form can ask "Was your grant
-- paid in advance?" first. With joint applicants, any one of you giving the notice and repaying counts for all (s 21(3)).

@export Must I give the Chief Commissioner notice and repay the grant because my transaction was not completed in time (s 20(2))?
GIVEN `the grant was paid to me before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid before the transaction was completed
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the transaction has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transaction has now been completed
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day it was completed (any day if it has not been)
      `the Chief Commissioner allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner allowed longer than 12 months from the commencement date for completion
      `the longer period ends on` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that longer period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` IF
        `the grant was paid to me before completion`
    AND `it was not completed within the period in` `the transaction` `or` `the longer period`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `a transaction from` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `the commencement date` `the completion date` `the transaction has been completed` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE
        `the longer period` MEANS IF `the Chief Commissioner allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the longer period ends on` ELSE NOTHING
        -- Only the dates and completion are read by s 20(2): the other facts are fixed placeholders.

@export By what day must I give notice and repay if my transaction is not completed in time (s 20(2))?
GIVEN `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner build the day laying the foundations began
      `the Chief Commissioner allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner allowed longer than 12 months from the commencement date for completion
      `the longer period ends on` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day of that longer period
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I repay if my transaction is not completed in time` IS
    `the last day to give notice and repay after` (`the period for completion ends on` `the transaction` `or` `the longer period`)
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `a transaction from` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `the commencement date` `the commencement date` FALSE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 0 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE
        `the longer period` MEANS IF `the Chief Commissioner allowed a longer period` THEN JUST `the longer period ends on` ELSE NOTHING
        -- Only the commencement date is read: the other facts are fixed placeholders.

@export By what day must I give notice and repay after learning that the total value is over the eligibility cap (s 20(2A))?
GIVEN `the day I became aware the total value exceeds or will exceed the cap` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware that the total value of the transaction is, or will be, more than the eligibility cap (this applies if the grant was paid before the cap could be checked)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I repay because my transaction is over the cap` IS
    `the last day to give notice and repay after` `the day I became aware the total value exceeds or will exceed the cap`

@export Must I give the Chief Commissioner notice and repay the grant because the residence requirement was not met (s 20(3))?
GIVEN `the grant was paid to me before I met the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid in anticipation of your living in the home for the required period
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was completed
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you moved in to live in the home as your main home
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day you began living in the home as your main home
      `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row you lived in the home as your main home
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your moving in more than 12 months after completion (s 12(3)(a))
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your living there for less than 12 months (s 12(3)(b))
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted you from the residence requirement (s 12(4))
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person applied for the grant with you
      `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the other person moved in as their main home
      `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day the other person began living in the home
      `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row the other person lived there
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start
      `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay
      `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement
      `there is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a further applicant
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay because I did not meet the residence requirement` IS
    `unless there is someone else` `there is someone else`
        (`known` (`the grant was paid to me before I met the residence requirement` AND `the residence requirement is not complied with by` (`the applicants from` `me` `the other person` `the other person is applying with me`) `completing on` `the completion date`))
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `an Australian citizen` `a clean history` EMPTY (`a residence from` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months I lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved my shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted me from the residence requirement`)
        `the other person` MEANS `an applicant from` 18 FALSE `an Australian citizen` `a clean history` EMPTY (`a residence from` `the other person lives, or will live, in the home` `the day the other person began, or will begin, living there` `the continuous months the other person lived, or will live, there` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's later start` `the Chief Commissioner approved the other person's shorter stay` `the Chief Commissioner exempted the other person from the residence requirement`)
        `a clean history` MEANS `a history from` `no` FALSE `no` `no`
        -- s 12 reads only the residence facts: age, status and history are fixed placeholders.

@export By what day must I give notice and repay if I do not meet the residence requirement (s 20(3))?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was completed
      `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you moved in to live in the home as your main home
      `the day I began, or will begin, living there` IS A DATE @desc The day you began living in the home as your main home
      `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner approved your moving in more than 12 months after completion (s 12(3)(a))
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I repay if I do not meet the residence requirement` IS
    `the last day to give notice and repay after` (`the period allowed for compliance with the residence requirement ends on` `the completion date` (`a residence from` `I live, or will live, in the home as my principal place of residence` `the day I began, or will begin, living there` 0 `the Chief Commissioner approved my later start` FALSE FALSE))
    -- The months lived, the shorter-stay approval and the exemption do not move the end of the period: placeholders.

@export What is the most I can be fined, in penalty units, for not giving the notice or not repaying as a condition requires (ss 20(4), 21(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for breaking a condition` IS
    `the maximum fine, in penalty units, for failing to comply with a condition of the grant`

§§ `s 45 -- what can be recovered from me`

-- These questions arise only if the Chief Commissioner may want the grant back.

@export Can the Chief Commissioner require me to repay the first home owner grant (ss 20, 45(1))?
GIVEN `the grant was paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you in error
      `the Chief Commissioner reversed the decision to pay it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has reversed the decision under which the grant was paid, for another reason
      `a condition of the grant requires me to repay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a condition of the grant (s 20 or one the Chief Commissioner imposed) now requires you to repay it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to repay the grant` IF
    `repayment can be required` `the grant was paid in error` `the Chief Commissioner reversed the decision to pay it` `a condition of the grant requires me to repay`

@export What is the most that can be recovered from me: the grant repaid, and the largest penalty on top (s 45)?
GIVEN `the grant paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the grant that was paid, in dollars
      `the grant was paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you in error
      `the Chief Commissioner reversed the decision to pay it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Chief Commissioner has reversed the decision under which the grant was paid, for another reason
      `a condition of the grant requires me to repay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a condition of the grant (s 20 or one the Chief Commissioner imposed) now requires you to repay it
      `it was paid as a result of dishonesty by an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid because of dishonesty by you or another applicant
      `I have not made a repayment that was required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to make a repayment required by the Chief Commissioner's notice or by a condition of the grant
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be recovered from me` IS
    `the amount to repay` PLUS `the most penalty under s 45(2)` `the amount to repay` `it was paid as a result of dishonesty by an applicant` `I have not made a repayment that was required`
    WHERE
        `the amount to repay` MEANS
            IF `repayment can be required` `the grant was paid in error` `the Chief Commissioner reversed the decision to pay it` `a condition of the grant requires me to repay`
            THEN `the grant paid to me`
            ELSE 0
